# Test: all five bus participant path forms (`/bgp/group/transit`, `/bgp/group/transit/peer/t1`, `/bgp/ip/<addr>`, `/bgp/peer/edge1`, `/bgp`) select exact peer sets, print as written, and reject unknown peer paths.
# QUESTION: with standalone peers `edge1` (127.0.0.2) and `lab` (127.0.0.3) and group
# `transit` containing `t1` (127.0.0.4) and `t2` (127.0.0.5), when `collector` is configured
# with each of `/bgp/group/transit`, `/bgp/group/transit/peer/t1`, `/bgp/ip/127.0.0.2`,
# `/bgp/peer/edge1`, and `/bgp` in `receive > from`, does `collector` receive events from
# exact peer sets (`{t1,t2}`, `{t1}`, `{edge1}`, `{edge1}`, `{edge1,lab,t1,t2}`), does
# `show config running` print each path verbatim as written, and is
# `receive { from [ /bgp/peer/nosuch ]; }` refused at `ze config validate` listing the
# configured peers? A unit test cannot decide this because it spans live BGP peer
# resolution in `DeliveryGraph`, config round-trip serialization in `show config running`,
# and full `ze config validate` diagnostics.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config S12 / AC-22, AC-6.
# PREVENTS: path-form resolution mismatches across group, grouped peer, IP alias,
# standalone peer, and `/bgp` root, or canonicalization rewriting the operator's written path.

option=timeout:value=180s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT

# Reusable peer scripts (one set per run so established-file markers stay distinct).
stdin=p-edge1-1:terminator=EOF_PE1_1
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65001
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.2
option=linger:value=true
option=established-file:path=e1-1.up
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.1.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.1
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PE1_1

stdin=p-lab-1:terminator=EOF_PL1_1
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65002
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.3
option=linger:value=true
option=established-file:path=lab-1.up
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.2.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.2
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PL1_1

stdin=p-t1-1:terminator=EOF_PT1_1
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65003
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.4
option=linger:value=true
option=established-file:path=t1-1.up
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.3.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.3
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PT1_1

stdin=p-t2-1:terminator=EOF_PT2_1
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65004
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.5
option=linger:value=true
option=established-file:path=t2-1.up
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.4.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.4
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PT2_1

stdin=p-edge1-2:terminator=EOF_PE1_2
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65001
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.2
option=linger:value=true
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.1.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.1
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PE1_2

stdin=p-lab-2:terminator=EOF_PL1_2
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65002
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.3
option=linger:value=true
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.2.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.2
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PL1_2

stdin=p-t1-2:terminator=EOF_PT1_2
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=60s
option=asn:value=65003
option=open:value=router-id:id=127.0.0.4
option=linger:value=true
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.3.0/24:next-hop=192.0.2.3
